      <p>Short in-town hops — DCA to Arlington's Crystal City, for instance — tend to favor Uber on price when conditions are calm, since the trip is short enough that even a moderate surge stays in a reasonable dollar range. Longer trips shift the math: DCA to Bethesda covers more distance and more variable traffic on the way, which is exactly the kind of trip where a rideshare estimate swings the most between a quiet Tuesday and a Friday rush-hour quote. Compare your specific route on both platforms at the time of day you'll actually be traveling, not at a random moment while planning — the numbers can differ substantially.</p>

